# Data & Flyway

## Schema

- All schema changes → new `V{n}__*.sql` under `db/migration/`.
- Non-test JPA: `ddl-auto: validate` only.
- Tables: `GO_<NAME>` uppercase; columns snake_case; include `ol`, audit columns, `deleted` when soft-deleting.

## Entities

- Extend `BaseEntity` (UUID string id, `@Version ol`, auditing).
- Soft delete: Hibernate `@SoftDelete` on the entity (not custom `@SQLDelete`/`@Where`).
- `repository.deleteById` performs soft delete when `@SoftDelete` is present.
- Relations: LAZY by default. Soft-deleted parent: `@NotFound(IGNORE)` like `ArticleEntity` — Hibernate **forces EAGER**, so do not also set `FetchType.LAZY`.
- Active-only uniqueness (users): partial unique index `WHERE deleted IS NOT TRUE` (see `V7__...`).

## Permission seeding (new features)

Do **not** rewrite old migrations. Prefer skill **add-flyway-migration**. New version should:

1. `INSERT` into `GO_PERMISSION` (`FEATURE_READ|CREATE|UPDATE|DELETE`)
2. Link ADMIN → all new perms in `GO_ROLE_PERMISSIONS`
3. Link USER → usually `*_READ` only (match article unless asked otherwise)

Follow id/style of `V2__init-auth-data.sql`.

## Repositories

- Spring Data interfaces only; `@EntityGraph` for paging/detail when fetching associations (see `ArticleRepository`).
